  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this proposal is to improve protection for tigers in the Forest Complex. This will be done by: 1. presenting an intense two-week ranger-led enforcement team leader course using PROTECT training materials to develop skilled enforcement leaders for the PAs; 2. holding a SMART software course for park based mangers (SMART Transitional Training) and mentoring park management and rangers on the use of the data collection techniques and analysis of the data; 3. donating essential field equipment for use by the rangers while on patrol; 4. accompanying rangers on patrols, identifying gaps in the their adoption of new techniques, and providing follow-up support; 5.a) continuing to conduct regular camera trapping and patrol-based monitoring in Thap Lan and Pang Sida to fill existing survey gaps in the complex, b) continuing long-term monitoring in areas with strong tiger presence, and c) providing on-the-job monitoring training to rangers; 6). organizing a 2 day workshop at Dong Yai Wildlife Sanctuary for 30 teachers from 15 schools adjacent to the complex on the design and implementation of conservation education modules and then tasking the trained teachers with developing and implementing a 1 week module at their home schools on local wildlife and the environment; and 7) sustaining support for community environmental patrols and training patrol members and planners within the community NGO.</narrative>
  </description>
